.env
.env.*
logs/
*.log
node_modules/
stress-project/tmp/
.claude/state/

# Reference corpus dropped into the repo root for analysis, 2026-08-16. This repo is PUBLIC and the
# build is closed at v1.0.0 with 80 tracked files (74 at closure, plus six audit documents added
# by the post-v1.0.0 audit on 2026-08-17); without this rule a `git add -A` would stage
# ~83,000 files and ~864MB of third-party source into it. The glob is deliberately a catch-all
# rather than an enumeration so a later upload following the same zip convention is covered before
# anyone thinks to add it. Present when this was written (16): agent-framework, babysitter,
# claude-agent-orchestration-guide, claude-agent-sdk-python, conductor, gastown, langgraph,
# mermaid-hybrid-stack-guide, neatcontext-plugins, oh-my-claudecode, open-code-review, OpenHands,
# ruflo, takt, turbo, zeroshot. None is a dependency: HC-5 still forbids installs, and these are
# read-only reference material navigated via Project-Explorer.md.
*-main/
*.pdf

# Third-party research reports dropped at the root alongside the corpus. Enumerated rather than
# globbed on *.md, because every root .md except these IS tracked and load-bearing (the plan,
# the ledgers, README, ROADMAP) - a glob here would hide the repo's own documentation.
deep-research-report.md

# Local-only working documents about that corpus and this build's history. Not published.
# The report is globbed rather than enumerated for the same reason the corpus above is: a second
# one arrived (ReportforClaudeWeb_2.txt, the audit distillation) and the literal filename rule did
# not cover it, so the file was unignored until someone noticed. The glob covers the next one too.
# Note the asymmetry with docs/audit/, which IS tracked: those are the audit's findings and belong
# in the repo, while these are working notes about material that never lands on GitHub at all.
ReportforClaudeWeb*.txt
Project-Explorer.md

# S6 planning output. Local until the operator promotes it: DIRECTORY_GUIDE.md is byte-pinned to the
# plan's §4.3 payload, so a tracked file the map does not name is the drift QR-DG-4 recorded, and the
# map can only gain a path through an upstream re-export. This mirrors how this build's own execution
# authority lives outside the repo with a copy inside.
PSYCHIC-CREW-LITE-PLAN.md

# R-SEC-1 (SECURITY-1, 2026-08-23). .claude/rules/security.md states that ".env, secrets/ and .ssh/
# are blocked by hooks/sensitive-guard.sh AND covered by .gitignore". The first half was true; the
# second was not — only .env and .env.* were listed here. The guard blocks WRITES through Write|Edit,
# which is one path in; a file arriving by any other route was neither ignored nor guarded, and a
# `git add -A` would have staged it into a repo whose remote is public.
#
# Found by the SECURITY-1 publication probe. The fix is to make the artifact match the rule rather
# than soften the rule to match the artifact.
secrets/
.ssh/
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
credentials.json
